    "title": "Prestin and the cochlear amplifier",
    "publication_year": 2006,
    "type": "article",
    "venue": "The Journal of Physiology",
    "cited_by_count": 145,
    "open_access": true,
    "abstract": "In non-mammalian, hair cell-bearing sense organs amplification is associated with mechano-electric transducer channels in the stereovilli (commonly called stereocilia). Because mammals possess differentiated outer hair cells (OHC), they also benefit from a novel electromotile process, powered by the motor protein, prestin. Here we consider new work pertaining to this protein and its potential role as the mammalian cochlear amplifier.",
